# PULSE MONOREPO AI GENERATION RULES

## Core Principles (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
1. NEVER alter existing architecture patterns, UI formats, or layouts found in the existing 78 files.
2. Carry forward ALL features while adding new ones. Do not drop existing functionality when editing or regenerating code.
3. ALWAYS use TypeScript strict mode.
4. NEVER introduce raw SQL; use Prisma Client (`@pulse/prisma`) exclusively.
5. Base all feature logic strictly on `pulse.txt`.

## Backend Pattern Rules (API)
- Controllers MUST use Express Router, Zod validation pipes (`validateBody`, `validateParams`), rate limiters (`rateLimiter.*`), and standard guards (`authGuard`, `adminGuard`).
- Services MUST log via `winston` (`logger.info`), interact with `@pulse/prisma`, and throw standard Errors handled by `error.filter.ts`.

## Frontend Pattern Rules (Web / Admin / Mobile)
- Next.js 14 App Router / React components MUST use Tailwind CSS, Lucide icons, and Axios (`@/lib/api`).
- State management MUST use Zustand.
- Do NOT alter UI color palettes or card formats established in `apps/web/src/components/feed/PollCard.tsx`.
- Flutter mobile code MUST match the defined widget structures.

## Execution Verification
No rushing, no guessing, no blind patching. Operate on facts only.
After creating or editing any files, ALWAYS run `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm build` in the terminal to ensure zero compilation or syntax errors before marking a task complete.